provenance.prompt:
Create one original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA production spritesheet for Moxie Capwell of Moonmorel Hex performing an eleven-pose right-facing basketball body-check push. Match the supplied Moxie portrait and gameplay references. She is an adult human woman with pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, long thick lavender high ponytail with small gold tie, purple-and-silver athletic uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-tops. Preserve face, eyes, ponytail, tie, mature human anatomy and outfit in every pose. No male, witch hat, beard, monster, robot or different person.

Draw polished, readable 1990s arcade basketball pixel-cel art. Exactly eleven distinct complete full-body Moxie figures in a 4-column by 3-row grid, row-major; bottom-right cell is transparent and empty. Broad true-transparent gutters and outer margin. Do not overlap or clip body, ponytail, hands or shoes. Show Moxie alone; no opponent or other character.

This is a legal stylized basketball body-check animation, not a punch or fight. Hands are open and empty and stay away from the face. The basketball is separate game art and never drawn; no ball, sphere, hoop, floor, court, shadows, glow, effects, text, labels or scenery.

0 stable defensive stance;
1 move laterally to close space;
2 bend knees and lower center of gravity;
3 shift into the opponent's path with shoulder turned sideways;
4 load the hips and plant both feet, arms held open for balance;
5 CONTACT at simulation tick8: a controlled shoulder-to-chest bump position, knees flexed, no punch, no grabbing; the hands stay apart and visible;
6 immediately recoil and stabilize, empty hands open;
7 slide one step as the unseen opponent is displaced offscreen;
8 regain stance;
9 move back into guard;
10 calm balanced recovery with both hands open.

All poses are connected and distinct; maintain a safe-looking athletic posture without violent facial expression or visible injury. Keep her recognizable face and lavender ponytail/gold tie clear, with no anatomy distortion. Return only true-transparent RGBA sprite art with alpha-zero background, no checkerboard, matte, haze, speckles or halo.
